-- Better Auth 1.7.0 added a required `issuer` column to `account` and a unique
-- index over (issuer, account_id); 1.7.3 withdrew both, and 1.7.7 never writes
-- the column — it checks the Drizzle schema at startup and refuses to run with
-- a NOT NULL column it will never fill. Its 1.7 upgrade guide for SQLite: drop
-- the index, then the column, in that order, because SQLite will not drop a
-- column an index still names. A new migration rather than an edit to 0000:
-- every database that ran 0000 has the column, and the journal is how they all
-- arrive at the same shape. Generated by `drizzle-kit generate` from the change
-- to `src/lib/server/db/auth.schema.ts`; only this comment was added.
DROP INDEX `account_issuer_accountId_uidx`;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE `account` DROP COLUMN `issuer`;